    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "This internet cable is as wide as a garden hose.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.69,
        "window": 4.17,
        "fill": 0.885
      },
      {
        "scene": "ask",
        "text": "How does the internet fit inside it?",
        "start": 4.47,
        "seconds": 2.3,
        "window": 2.63,
        "fill": 0.875
      },
      {
        "scene": "open",
        "text": "Slice it open. Past its protective layers sit glass fibres, each about as thin as a human hair.",
        "start": 7.1,
        "seconds": 6.84,
        "window": 7.33,
        "fill": 0.933
      },
      {
        "scene": "light",
        "text": "Your video races down one as flashes of light, bouncing off the glass walls from one continent to the next.",
        "start": 14.43,
        "seconds": 7.02,
        "window": 7.63,
        "fill": 0.92
      },
      {
        "scene": "map",
        "text": "And it is not alone. Over 1.5M kilometres of cable cross the seabed, with more than 600 cables working or planned.",
        "start": 22.07,
        "seconds": 9.3,
        "window": 9.93,
        "fill": 0.937
      },
      {
        "scene": "danger",
        "text": "But down here, what keeps breaking them? Mostly fishing gear and ship anchors dragged across the cable.",
        "start": 32.0,
        "seconds": 6.35,
        "window": 6.93,
        "fill": 0.916
      },
      {
        "scene": "fix",
        "text": "So a repair ship lifts the broken ends onto its deck and joins the glass back together.",
        "start": 38.93,
        "seconds": 5.82,
        "window": 6.27,
        "fill": 0.928
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "Roughly 200 times a year, a cable breaks somewhere. Yet your video keeps playing, because the data takes another cable.",
        "start": 45.2,
        "seconds": 8.02,
        "window": 8.67,
        "fill": 0.925
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "Right now, your next video is racing through this cable.",
